WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.000
Visual hierarchy is the invisible force in every design you've seen.

2
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:14.000
It's what tells your eyes where to go — in a deliberate order.

3
00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:24.667
When you look at a poster, you don't process it all at once.

4
00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:30.667
Your eyes move through it in a sequence. That was designed.

5
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.000
SIZE: bigger elements get seen first. A headline is big for a reason.

6
00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:46.667
WEIGHT: bold text commands attention before regular weight.

7
00:00:46.833 --> 00:00:52.333
COLOR: high contrast screams. Low contrast whispers.

8
00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:58.333
SPACING: isolated elements feel more important than clustered ones.

9
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:04.000
Great designers control attention. Hierarchy is how they do it.

10
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.667
Learn graphic design at 0xverse Academy.

